================================================================================
                           AmitOS — Falcon Edition
                              Version 1.0 | amd64
                     Built on Debian 12 (Bookworm) | 2026-06-14
================================================================================

ABOUT
-----
AmitOS is a custom, Debian-based Linux distribution designed for everyday users
who demand a beautiful, fast, and reliable computing experience. Built on the
rock-solid foundation of Debian 12 "Bookworm", AmitOS ships with a curated
set of applications, a polished GNOME desktop environment, and sensible defaults
so you can be productive right from the first boot.

The "Falcon" release marks the debut of AmitOS — soaring high with performance
optimizations, full multimedia support, and a clean out-of-the-box experience.


FEATURES
--------
  * Polished GNOME desktop with custom AmitOS theme and icon set
  * Full multimedia support (codecs, VLC, Rhythmbox included)
  * Privacy and security hardened defaults (UFW firewall enabled)
  * ZRAM swap enabled for improved memory performance
  * Fast boot via systemd optimization
  * Comprehensive hardware support (Realtek, Broadcom, NVIDIA drivers)
  * LibreOffice suite for productivity
  * GIMP and Shotwell for photo management
  * Thunderbird for email
  * Firefox ESR as default web browser


SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
-------------------
  Minimum:
    CPU     : 64-bit dual-core processor (x86_64)
    RAM     : 2 GB
    Storage : 20 GB free disk space
    Display : 1024 x 768 resolution

  Recommended:
    CPU     : 64-bit quad-core processor
    RAM     : 4 GB or more
    Storage : 40 GB or more (SSD preferred)
    Display : 1920 x 1080 (Full HD)


DEFAULT APPLICATIONS
--------------------
  Web Browser      : Firefox ESR
  Office Suite     : LibreOffice (Writer, Calc, Impress, Draw)
  File Manager     : GNOME Files (Nautilus)
  Terminal         : GNOME Terminal
  Text Editor      : GNOME Text Editor
  Music Player     : Rhythmbox
  Photo Manager    : Shotwell
  Video Player     : VLC Media Player
  Image Editor     : GIMP
  Email Client     : Thunderbird
  Disk Manager     : GParted
  Package Manager  : Synaptic + GNOME Software Center
  System Monitor   : GNOME System Monitor


INSTALLATION
------------
  1. Download the AmitOS ISO from the official GitHub releases page.
  2. Flash the ISO to a USB drive (minimum 4 GB) using:
       - Balena Etcher (recommended, cross-platform)
       - dd command: sudo dd if=amitos-1.0-amd64.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress
  3. Boot from the USB drive (press F12/F11/Del at POST for boot menu).
  4. Select "Install AmitOS" or "Try AmitOS Live" from the GRUB menu.
  5. Follow the on-screen Calamares installer for guided installation.
  6. Reboot after installation and enjoy AmitOS!


POST-INSTALL SETUP
------------------
  Update the system:
    sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

  Install additional drivers (if needed):
    sudo apt install firmware-linux firmware-linux-nonfree

  Enable additional repositories:
    sudo dpkg --add-architecture i386
    sudo apt update

  Check AmitOS version:
    cat /usr/share/amitos/version


